 [17592186395784 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395784 1084 #uuid "05fd7882-e12b-5d1e-bda2-674211a5aad1" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395785 1081 "2" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395785 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395785 1084 #uuid "61e0f80f-69b1-578c-857a-82bc0682835a" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395786 1081 "1" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395786 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395786 1084 #uuid "26a77c96-4bef-5e82-8889-1c4a9ce7d523" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395787 1081 "0" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395787 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395787 1084 #uuid "9c9b090b-3cbc-511c-95ab-35fc8c1fc057" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395788 1081 "-1" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395788 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395788 1084 #uuid "d1c50146-0d7c-501d-bf37-4d8d838c3cef" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395789 1068 #edb/ref 17592186395790 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395789 1069 "q-21496" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395789 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395789 1071 "For which value of $x$ does the function $f(x)={x}^{3}+\\frac{48}{x}$ defined for $x\\in (0,\\infty )$ have a local minimum?" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395789 1072 #uuid "6bb098c4-0b9d-56fe-8eb4-70ba83a986f8" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395789 1074 "First, we find the stationary points. Differentiating $f(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =3{x}^{2}-\\frac{48}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving for ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ on $(0,\\infty )$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-\\frac{48}{{x}^{2}} & =0 \\\\ 3{x}^{4}-48 & =0 \\\\ 3({x}^{4}-16) & =0 \\\\ 3({x}^{2}+4)({x}^{2}-4) & =0 \\\\ 3({x}^{2}+4)(x+2)(x-2) & =0 \\\\ x & =\\pm 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $x=2$ is a stationary point on $(0,\\infty ).$ Next, to determine whether this point is a local maximum or minimum, we use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's choose the test points $x=1,3$ and evaluate the first derivative at these points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1) & =3(1)^{2}-\\frac{48}{{1}^{2}}=-45<0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(3) & =3(3)^{2}-\\frac{48}{{3}^{2}}=27-\\frac{16}{3}=\\frac{65}{3}>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe summarize the information in a table, shown below.\n\n| $x$ | $(0,2)$ | $2$ | $(2,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Test Point | $1$ |  | $3$ |\n| ${f}^{′}$ | $-$ | $0$ | $+$ |\n| $f$ | $↘$ | min | $↗$ |\n\nFinally, let's use the table above to classify the critical point.\n\n- At $x=2,$ the first derivative changes sign from negative to positive. Therefore, $x=2$ is a local minimum.\n\nWe conclude that $f(x)$ has a local minimum at $x=2.$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395790 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395791 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395790 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395792 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395790 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395793 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395790 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395794 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395790 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395795 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395790 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395790 1077 "selection" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395790 1079 #edb/ref 17592186395792 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395790 1080 #uuid "5e6ea143-756a-5eb6-a6ed-9e3449dbdb6b" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395791 1081 "\\sqrt{2}" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395791 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395791 1084 #uuid "220c4644-028c-5dcb-955d-3b2d5604dc62" 13194139533466 1759218