 for the sphere and then differentiate it using implicit differentiation. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =\\frac{4}{3}\\pi {r}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(V) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{4}{3}\\pi {r}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}r}(\\frac{4}{3}\\pi {r}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot 4\\pi {r}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=1$ and $r=2,$ and solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =1\\cdot 4\\pi (2)^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =16\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the balloon is increasing at a rate of $16\\pi {\\text{ cm}}^{3}\\text{/s}$\n when the radius is $2\\,\\text{cm}.$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395797 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395798 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395797 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395799 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395797 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395800 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395797 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395801 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395797 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395802 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395797 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395797 1077 "selection" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395797 1079 #edb/ref 17592186395799 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395797 1080 #uuid "86b9d34d-27a9-54ed-b870-554479215d16" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395798 1081 "8\\pi \\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}\\text{/s}" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395798 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395798 1084 #uuid "b1ea5dbf-e0e0-5b87-9716-69e18e732d25" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395799 1081 "16\\pi \\,{\\text