R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are two pivot columns (the $2$nd and the $3$rd). Thus, ${x}_{1}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we obtain ${x}_{3}=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get ${x}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{1}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting, for instance, ${x}_{1}=1,$ we get the eigenvector\n$v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395845 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395846 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395845 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395847 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395845 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395848 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395845 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395849 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395845 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395850 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395845 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395845 1077 "selection" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395845 1079 #edb/ref 17592186395847 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395845 1080 #uuid "307532aa-e20c-56a5-8f44-7fdbefdbc75e" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395846 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395846 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395846 1084 #uuid "4804a85a-1639-5fa2-9795-6c51af17adc7" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395847 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395847 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395847 1084 #uuid "3e1a8aa3-46ff-5b95-94c5-aa562df4b40b" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395848 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\